IO-41: reject a malformed number in a math expression

The expression tokenizers (math/MathExpr.cpp for control rules and [GWF],
quality/Treatment.cpp for [TREATMENT]) convert the characters of a number
with std::stod, which reads the longest valid prefix ("2.5E+" -> 2.5,
"1.5.2" -> 1.5) and throws std::invalid_argument when there is none ("."),
which nothing caught, so the program terminated. Treat a number that stod
does not consume completely as an error: the tokenizer reports it and
mathexpr::parse() fails (an empty expression still parses, as before); the
treatment validator reports it as a malformed number.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-41_swmm600.patch

